  "notes": "Symmetric two-unit duplex: cream stucco upper floor over a sandy-tan ground floor with a terracotta brick plinth (#d9946f), each unit carrying a smooth WHITE cantilevered box (#f0f1f5) on floor 1 (schema gap: these boxes project ~0.5m proud of the facade and their underside is visible; modelled here only as flat colour bands). Full-height tan pilaster strip at the party line, big cream fascia with the right roof plane stepped slightly higher than the left (schema gap: per-volume height offset). Two dark charcoal doors (#3b3a3e) with small intercom boxes beside them. Frontage: low rendered tan wall (#dfc499) that reads as smooth STUCCO not brick (wall.type gap), topped by a run of faceted green hedge blocks (#78a24c light / #486030 shadow — hedge prop pending); cream-white horizontal-slat pedestrian gate (#f4ebda, 'slat' style gap) beside a cream intercom pillar (#ede4d0) at the far left; spec notes say twin gates so a second identical gate likely sits off-frame right. Smooth terracotta entry paths (#d9946f) to each door, a low tan planter with grass at the right entry, and a terracotta crazy-paving flagstone driveway apron (#eda47e, joints #c7968c) crossing the grey concrete sidewalk toward the right; two dark round manhole covers in sidewalk and road. Sampled colours from 24x18 grids 2026-07-03."
